// An edge fires ONCE; a level fires every cycle it holds. Same option slot, and
// the trigger word is the whole difference -- so the two counters below drift
// apart by exactly the number of cycles the pin stays high.
//
// Not every part has a level trigger. STM32's EXTI has rising and falling and
// nothing else, so csp_board_irq_attach refuses `high` there and the source
// stays quiet rather than firing on something the silicon substituted.
#digital Sig  in high   2:5
#digital Ping in rising 2:6

#variable Held = 0        // cycles the level was asserted
#variable Edges = 0       // times the edge arrived

Held = Held + 1 ? Sig.fired
Edges = Edges + 1 ? Ping.fired
